  "aiden-basset": {
    title: "VC Operations",
    currentName: "Aiden Basset",
    currentMeta: "VC Operations | 2026",
    whatToKnow: `
      <strong>Key Contacts</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A.S.</strong> &mdash; funds food and sometimes materials. Contact <strong>Chris</strong> by email</li>
        <li><strong>SLBO</strong> &mdash; buys the food, and handles purchases, expenses, and reimbursements. Contact <strong>Alma</strong> through TAP or email. Check with the SLBO Fund Manager before answering vendor questions about payment</li>
        <li><strong>CSI</strong> &mdash; advisor for non-food, non-money matters. Contact <strong>Maria</strong> through TAP or email</li>
        <li>Email and TAP are the best lines of contact; schedule a meeting with any of the three if something is unclear</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Due Dates Calendar</strong>
      <p>Until A.S. changes the rules:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Friday, 5 weeks before event</strong> &mdash; Programming App due</li>
        <li><strong>21 days before event</strong> &mdash; TAP Form due</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A.S.'s calendar of funding due dates aligns with the academic calendar &mdash; <strong>funding weeks start on Mondays and end on Sundays</strong>. If the Spring Week 6 and Week 7 due dates are both Friday of Spring Week 1 at 11:59pm, you can set the deadlines for when you want events submitted by the other board members. This will help when people are missing invoices and you need to ask them for it.</p>

      <strong>Programming Apps</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>What files are needed, what info is needed, etc. &mdash; see the A.S. funding guide</li>
        <li>Read <strong>all</strong> of the funding guide (except tournament funding)</li>
        <li>The app is your best play at VCO; it has a good rubric for most of the information you'll eventually know by heart</li>
        <li>An event is eligible for A.S. Funding if:
          <ul>
            <li>The event is on campus</li>
            <li>It is open to all UCSD undergraduate students</li>
            <li>It is open to only UCSD undergraduate students, graduate students, faculty, and staff</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <strong>PEEFS</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Fill out PEEFS &mdash; your programming app will be denied if you are not filling out PEEFS</li>
        <li>Join the A.S. Town Hall Discord for feedback and to ask the things you don't need to ask publicly; don't ask questions in the main Discord &mdash; email Chris or message him directly</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>TAP Forms</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Needed for all the information from the programming app, plus general knowledge about the event</li>
        <li>The TAP form for an event must be <strong>started and confirmation submitted 21 days before</strong> the event, and the final version must be <strong>submitted by 14 days before</strong> the event</li>
        <li>Use only approved vendors (e.g., Amazon, tap.ucsd.edu/vendor)</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Reimbursements (A.S. Funding)</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>You still have SLBO buy most of your food from events, but for doing by one of the officers helping run the event, however some vendors such as Vons, Costco, or Amazon require you to file for reimbursement because SLBO cannot easily go and pay for an invoiced order:
          <ul>
            <li>This is when one of the <strong>principal members</strong> (should be all exec officers) will purchase the items on their card, then be reimbursed later</li>
            <li><strong>You still need to apply for A.S. funding for reimbursement</strong> &mdash; fill out the questionnaire accordingly and you should see the reimbursement module pop up instead of the vendors one</li>
            <li>Fill out the module and have the paying Principal Member (PM) apply for reimbursement as is instructed</li>
            <li><strong>Submitting for reimbursement is due within 7 days after the event, but do the application ASAP so nothing falls through the cracks</strong></li>
            <li>A reimbursement is a good way to still get funding for non-traditional vendors (have been used in the past for a Valentine's Day card making event), or as a last-resort backup to resolve problems with a stingy vendor not giving you an invoice, however try to use it as little as possible so that no money has to come out of anyone's account and no payments fall through the cracks</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <strong>VTools</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Our way of getting funding from the <strong>SD Section</strong> of big IEEE (<code>events.vtools.ieee.org/tego_/events/administration</code>)</li>
        <li>Fill out VTools forms for events both future and past, but only for events big IEEE would care about (workshops, GBMs, outreach &mdash; not necessarily social events)</li>
        <li>Unless the event explicitly allows public attendance (meaning it wouldn't be A.S. funded), <strong>do not allow registration</strong>. The typical workaround is to set registration from an arbitrary date weeks ago through yesterday (or day-of if the event has passed) so technically registration dates exist but no one can sign up</li>
        <li>Not every tab needs to be filled &mdash; include what someone from SD Section would care to know about the event</li>
        <li><strong>Make sure you have attendance records from the event</strong> &mdash; you'll need them for PEEFS too</li>
      </ul>
    `,
