    currentName: "Cailey Murad",
    currentMeta: "Social Chair | 2026",
    whatToKnow: `
      <strong>Organizing Events</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Start planning as early as possible &mdash; deadlines creep up fast. Miss a deadline and there won't be any events</li>
        <li>Expect around <strong>20&ndash;25 people</strong> per event</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Event Ideas</strong>
      <p><strong>Quarterly:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Pizza and Board Game Night</li>
        <li>Study Jam with Boba (twice a quarter)</li>
        <li>Fundraisers: Bake Sale, Yogurt World Fundraiser + Meet the Board</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Holiday:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Pumpkin Carving Night</li>
        <li>Gingerbread House Showdown</li>
        <li>Valentine's Day Crafting &amp; Gifting (cards, bouquets, chocolates)</li>
        <li>3.14 Pi Day Party</li>
        <li>Earth Day Party (swap meet, sustainability, houseplants)</li>
        <li>Mother's Day Crafting &amp; Gift Giving (cards, painted canvases)</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Annual:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Bonfire &amp; S'mores at La Jolla Shores</li>
        <li>Ultimate Scavenger Hunt</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Other:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Movie Night at Price Theatre</li>
        <li>Create Your Own Keychain</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Get creative! There's a lot of material left over from past events (utensils, decor, etc.) that can be reused.</p>

      <strong>AS Funding Rules</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>ONLY</strong> use a credit card from an executive board member for AS-funded events. Do NOT use your personal credit card</li>
        <li>If collaborating with another club, one club can use AS funding and the other can use personal cards</li>
        <li>Invoices don't need credit card info and dates don't need to be exact</li>
        <li>Do not exceed the budget</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Room Options</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Henry Booker Room (Jacobs Hall 2512)</li>
        <li>Price Center &mdash; only VC Events can book these rooms</li>
        <li>For food events, book EBU1 or a classroom at Price Center</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Event Submissions</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit events about a quarter of the way into the quarter, every Monday</li>
        <li>Check in with VC Operations for submission deadlines</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>After the Event</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Clean the room completely and take out the trash (there should be access to a vacuum and cleaning supplies through another door)</li>
      </ul>
    `,
