  "loraine-diosa": {
    title: "Marketing Chair",
    currentName: "Loraine Diosa",
    currentMeta: "Marketing Chair | 2026",
    whatToKnow: `
      <strong>Overview of Duties</strong>
      <p>At a high level, your role is to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Capture content (photos/videos) at events</li>
        <li>Create recap posts (collages, videos, etc.)</li>
        <li>Manage and contribute to IEEE's social media presence</li>
        <li>Help promote events and maintain engagement</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You're also expected to be present and involved as a general board member.</p>

      <strong>Weekly Expectations</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>OAH (Office/Activity Hours):</strong> ~2 hours/week</li>
        <li><strong>Internal Meetings:</strong> ~1 hour/week</li>
        <li><strong>Events:</strong> varies, 1&ndash;3 hours depending on schedule</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Stay consistent with meetings and keep up through Slack.</p>

      <strong>Marketing Chair Responsibilities</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Bi-Quarterly All Hands (1&ndash;3 hours)</li>
        <li>Quarterly GBMs (1&ndash;3 hours) &mdash; recap videos &amp; collages</li>
        <li>Posting on Instagram &amp; Discord (~1 hour)</li>
        <li>Attending events / taking pictures &amp; videos (1&ndash;3 hours)</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Content Creation</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Take photos and videos at events</li>
        <li>Make recap collages or short videos</li>
        <li>Post content on Instagram and Discord</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Posting</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Instagram posts + stories</li>
        <li>Discord Newsletter announcements (same as posts) &mdash; extra step: create an event on Discord</li>
      </ul>
      <p>On average this is ~30 min&ndash;1 hour per week, varies with events.</p>

      <strong>Tools &amp; Access</strong>
      <p>Make sure you get access to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Instagram Account</strong> (posting access)</li>
        <li><strong>Discord Admin Permissions</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Slack Channels</strong> &mdash; important ones: <code>2026-2027-board</code>, <code>26-27-internal</code>, <code>pr</code>, <code>z-play</code> (for posting media)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Use Slack actively to stay updated and share content.</p>

      <strong>Key Documents</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>IEEE Drive &mdash; for storing content and materials</li>
        <li>Slack &mdash; main communication + media sharing</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Tips &amp; Best Practices</strong>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Take more content than you think you need.</strong> You'll always use it later &mdash; better to have extra than not enough</li>
        <li><strong>Stay consistent with posting.</strong> Even simple posts help keep engagement up</li>
        <li><strong>Don't overthink content.</strong> It doesn't need to be perfect, just clear, fun, and representative of the event and org</li>
        <li><strong>Communicate with your co-chair.</strong> Split responsibilities (who posts, who edits, who covers which event) so nothing gets overwhelming</li>
        <li><strong>Be present at events.</strong> Some of the best content comes naturally when you're actively engaged</li>
      </ol>

      <strong>Final Remarks</strong>
      <p>This role is what you make of it &mdash; as creative, involved, and fun as you want. Once you get into the rhythm of capturing content and posting, it becomes pretty natural. Good luck!</p>
    `,
