    title: "Supercomputing Chair",
    currentName: "Gauri Renjith",
    currentMeta: "Supercomputing Chair | 2026",
    whatToKnow: `
      <strong>Overview</strong>
      <p>The Supercomputing Chair is the primary liaison between UCSD Supercomputing and IEEE. UCSD Supercomputing is technically a subcommunity of UCSD IEEE, so IEEE manages key logistics like TAP forms and marketing support. The Chair also represents Supercomputing at IEEE events and helps promote it.</p>

      <strong>Election Process</strong>
      <ol>
        <li>Get selected through the Supercomputing election process</li>
        <li>Present and get formally elected during IEEE general elections</li>
      </ol>

      <strong>IEEE Meetings</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>All-Hands</strong> &mdash; 2&times; per quarter with all IEEE board members. Share major updates and stay informed on IEEE-wide developments</li>
        <li><strong>IEEE GBM</strong> &mdash; 1&times; per quarter event for the larger engineering student body. Make sure the Supercomputing information is relevant and engaging, and have yourself (or another Supercomputing officer) present the slides</li>
        <li><strong>Projects Meetings</strong> &mdash; more frequent at the VC of Projects' discretion; communicate all relevant Supercomputing updates and needs to IEEE</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Open Access Hours &amp; Tabling</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Hold <strong>2 hours/week</strong> at the IEEE project space (can typically be used as work time)</li>
        <li>IEEE tables in the first few weeks of each quarter (Library Walk, Engineering on the Green) &mdash; all IEEE officers are expected to be involved</li>
        <li>Rule of thumb: each Supercomputing officer does ~2 hours of tabling (especially in Fall)</li>
        <li>Arrange additional Supercomputing-only tabling before Winter GBM if possible (coordinate with VCP)</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Supercomputing Officer Meetings</strong>
      <p>Attend Supercomputing officer meetings and stay up to date on all activities.</p>

      <strong>Event Planning &amp; Logistics</strong>
      <p>Manage AS funding and logistics for major events:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Supercomputing GBM</strong> in Winter Quarter</li>
        <li><strong>SBCC</strong> (Days 1&ndash;3, each day counts as an event)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Responsibilities include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Obtaining <strong>official food invoices</strong></li>
        <li>Coordinating <strong>room bookings</strong> (e.g., with SDSC)</li>
        <li>Submitting all materials to IEEE VP Operations on time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Plan these events (and any other Supercomputing events needing food) at least <strong>one quarter in advance</strong>; keep the Supercomputing officers on track.</p>

      <strong>Marketing &amp; Promotion</strong>
      <p>Make sure all events and SCC team applications are promoted across IEEE platforms (Instagram, Discord, etc.). Work with the marketing/design team for flyers, or create them yourself.</p>

      <strong>Publicity &amp; Outreach</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Reach out to IEEE San Diego and IEEE Computer Society for funding opportunities (SCC, SBCC, etc.); coordinate with VC Finance</li>
        <li>Work with VP External to understand what Supercomputing information is in the IEEE sponsorship package; reach out to IEEE company contacts for partnerships when possible</li>
        <li>Supercomputing runs its own company outreach &mdash; keep the Supercomputing outreach officer informed and involved</li>
        <li>After major Supercomputing milestones, attend or send a representative to IEEE Executive Committee meetings and ECE faculty/alumni events</li>
        <li>Key that UCSD departments (CSE, ECE, HDSI, SCIDS, etc.) are <strong>aware</strong> of Supercomputing's accomplishments. Coordinate with President or VCP to arrange this</li>
      </ul>

      <strong>Main Expectations</strong>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strong communication</strong> &mdash; actively bridge IEEE and Supercomputing; attend and contribute to both sets of meetings. Stay active on Slack</li>
        <li><strong>Stay up-to-date</strong> &mdash; be aware and reasonably knowledgeable about everything Supercomputing does and what high-performance computing means (you'll need to answer questions)</li>
      </ul>
    `,
